  [1mThe change, in [38;5;153mauth.js[39m:[0m if [38;5;153mREPORTS_TOKEN[39m is set, a request with [38;5;153mAuthorization: Bearer <token>[39m is let through. Logging
  in with the session cookie still works the same way. If [38;5;153mREPORTS_TOKEN[39m isn't set, the token route is off and only login
  works.

  [1mTested by running the server locally (with a test token) and calling the route:[0m
